nethack newbie <nethack.new...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> 1. =A0What are the priorities for a Barbarian in the early game?
>
> I've been playing a Barbarian off and on for several months now. =A0I
> never seem to get very far, made it to Medusa only once. =A0I know I
> need to change my approach, but am not sure what is most important.

What I call the early game ends when you've finished the mines
and sokoban.  If you've made it to Medusa once, then you've got
a reasonably good idea of what the priorities are.  At each death
puzzle over what you'd been doing the past several levels to see
if you've been rushing through levels, or if any other change in
strategy is called for.  Sounds like you've already learned plenty
of tactics.

> 2. =A0When people talk about clearing out the Mines, are they really
> clearing everything and testing all weapons/armor/items for BUC? =A0I
> test some stuff when it's convenient, but I get bored trying on that
> 10th pair of iron shoes =A0. . . =A0I read that most people haul stuff up
> to the Minetown altar to test for BUC. =A0Are they really hauling
> everything up?

Everything includes boulders.  Okay, everything includes rocks
but not boulders.  I only haul rocks to the minetown shrine if I
plan on killing the cross-aligned priest.  If you run out of throwing
rocks and the priest is still alive, you didn't haul 300+ rocks there.
Other than rock, yes I haul all items up or down to the altar as
long as I continue working the mines.

Yes, it's boring trying on lots of shoes.  Try them on anyways.
The one time you find an uncursed +3 iron boots at will have
been worth it.  No matter my current armor I try on all blessed
armor items and all items that might be useful because of their
type.

> 3. =A0Is it worth trying to keep my exp level low, letting my pet kill
> almost everything, and then buying protection in Minetown? =A0I fail at
> this so often, that I'm thinking it should only be played by Healers.

Not if the priest is cross aligned and you expect to kill him.
If the priest is cross-aligned, it's a matter of personal tastes.

